    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1093">

                <pb facs="1135" n="1123" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/6–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Churchill</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Truman </hi><anchor
                        n="84" xml:id="d1093-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-31">May 31, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. In the light of the deteriorating situation in the Levant States, His
                    Majesty’s Government felt bound to order the Commander-in-Chief of the Middle
                    East to intervene, in order to prevent further <pb facs="1136" n="1124"
                        xml:id="pg1124"/> effusion of blood. My immediately following message<anchor
                        n="85" xml:id="d1093-f2"/> contains the statement on the subject which the
                    Foreign Secretary has just made in the House of Commons.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d1093-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Owing to the urgency, His Majesty’s Government felt they could not wait longer
                    for your reply to my message No. 59 but I feel sure that I may count on the
                    support of United States Government for the steps which we have felt bound to
                    take.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
